## Fixture 3, "The default surface": a block holding a
## parameterized Surface "matte" Kd 0.1 around one sphere at x=1.2, then an
## un-surfaced sphere at x=-1.2 after AttributeEnd, which falls back to
## defaultSurfaceShader's matte with no explicit parameters (Kd 1). No
## ambient light leaves Ka unused, so brightness is linear in Kd exactly as
## in the plastic fixtures, and a correct render puts the parameterized
## sphere's red channel near a tenth of the default one's. A build that
## shares one shader instance's parameter list across calls would still
## hold the block's Kd 0.1 list when the un-surfaced sphere shades, under
## both renderers, so both come out dim instead of one bright. Not
## third-party.
Display "surfaceparameters_default.tif" "file" "rgba"
Format 200 100 1
Projection "perspective" "fov" [45]
Clipping 0.5 50
Translate 0 0 5
WorldBegin
LightSource "distantlight" 1 "intensity" [1.0] "lightcolor" [1 1 1]
	"from" [0 0 -5] "to" [0 0 0]
AttributeBegin
	Translate 1.2 0 0
	Surface "matte" "Ka" [0.2] "Kd" [0.1]
	Sphere 1 -1 1 360
AttributeEnd
Translate -1.2 0 0
Sphere 1 -1 1 360
WorldEnd
